Undo a recent destructive mutation by its id (~60s window), or a whole `--all` run by its job id (for an hour after the job ends).

The mutation id is printed by `archive`, `trash`, `spam`, `mark-read`, `read-archive` and `desk done`; copy it from there. `archive --all` and its siblings print a job id instead. Undoing a job is a background job of its own: this command waits for it and says how many messages came back, and how many it had to skip.

Usage: mxr undo [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>


Options:
      --dry-run
          Show which undo would run without mutating state

      --format <FORMAT>
          [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
